  "preamble": "Depalatalization (hardening) of the palatalized bilabial nasal [mʲ] to plain [m]. Palatalized labials are perceptually weak word-finally, and Belarusian hardened them there: Old East Slavic семь (13th c. /ˈsʲɛːmʲ/) 'seven' keeps its soft labial in standard Russian [sʲemʲ] but has hard [m] in Belarusian сем [sʲem]; Old East Slavic осмь 'eight' likewise gives Belarusian восем.",
